      }
    },
    "c6": {
      "anchor": "words#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "8. Words",
      "excerpt": "The idea Words used today Recommended Why Spell UI's pieces, <card> , <menu> com",
      "text": "I think \"alias\" is fine as english, not clear what your other examples refer to.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-21T01:44:36.534Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "short name, quoted phrase",
      "offset": 1034,
      "edited": "2026-11-21T01:45:42.335Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-21T01:55:21.799Z",
          "html": "<p>Kept \"alias\". Its row now lists the four things it names, each with a real line: a template's other name (<code>aka \"playing card\"</code>, Spanish <code>alias \"carta\"</code>); quoted words that become a phrase (<code>it \"is a face card\" if ...</code>); the hover's \"variable it · alias\"; and the parser's own rule aliases, which people never see.</p>\n<p>A person meets the first three, and one word fits them all. Where they need telling apart: a template's alias, a quoted alias.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-21T01:47:06.352Z"
      }
    },
